TypeScript sources: a .ts or .mts module (entry, import, service) is loaded with
its types erased to whitespace by swc_ts_fast_strip in strip-only mode, padded to
each erased character's UTF-8 width, so lines and columns in errors and stacks
still point into the .ts file. Extensionless and .js imports reach a .ts file
when no .js exists; the watcher and typings scan see .ts too.

